Have you looked at http://www.lojban.org/tiki/wavelessonscontinued , which
is now the recommended learning material? While I had a background in
predicate logic before coming to Lojban, I find your claim to be patently
false. In particular I find that even the CLL, which is a very poor
learning material in the first place, assumes no background in predicate
logic, even though it would be somewhat easier to read that way. The WLC is
far better in this regard, albeit a little bit incomplete.

